    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Abstract"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 49,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 94.667, 486.043, 517.0, 575.0 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We consider a family of Pfaﬃan Schur processes whose ﬁrst coordinate marginal relates to the half– space geometric last passage percolation. We show that the line ensembles corresponding to the Pfaﬃan Schur processes with geometric weights converge uniformly over compact sets to the Airy line ensemble. By detailed asymptotic analysis of the kernels, we can verify the conditions for the ﬁnite dimensional weak convergence introduced in [7]. By utilizing the tightness criteria of the line ensembles established in [8], we can further improve the ﬁnite dimensional convergence to the uniform convergence over compact sets. Moreover, using the same methodology we also show that sequences of spiked Pfaﬃan Schur processes converge uniformly over compact sets to the Airy wanderer line ensembles constructed in [7]."
  }, {
