    "bounding box" : [ 70.333, 121.333, 542.333, 195.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In recent years, models related to KPZ growth in a half-space were extensively studied. For example, [1] studied the ﬂuctuations of last passage percolation with exponential weights in a half-quadrant within the framework of Pfaﬃan Schur processes, [17] shows the ﬂuctuations of a one-dimensional polynuclear growth model in a half-space, the log-gamma polymer in a half space was also considered [13]. For a large amount of half-space models, the ﬂuctuations follow the GUE Tracy Widom distribution in the bulk. It is interesting to further investigate if these models converges to the Airy line ensemble. The Airy line ensemble Airy is a random sequence of continuous functions that arises as a scaling limit"
